## 3. GRAPHICS PIPELINE CONFIGURATION

### Post-Processing Stack Order
```
RenderPass → EffectComposer → UnrealBloomPass → OutputPass
```

### Parameter Values (Tuned for Retro-Futurism)
| Pass | Parameter | Value | Rationale |
|------|-----------|-------|-----------|
| **UnrealBloom** | threshold | 0.85 | Only brightest surfaces glow (emissive materials) |
| | strength | 1.4 | Neon intensity without washing out colors |
| | radius | 0.35 | Tight bloom, not bloated halos |
| | resolution | 256 | Performance balance (full res = expensive) |
| **Output** | toneMapping | THREE.ReinhardToneMapping | Prevents overexposure on bright surfaces |
| | outputEncoding | THREE.sRGBEncoding | Standard color space for web display |

### Procedural Texture Generation Math

#### Alien Sprite Canvas (per type)
```javascript
function generateAlienCanvas(type, frameIndex): HTMLCanvasElement {
  const canvas = document.createElement('canvas');
  canvas.width = 64; canvas.height = 32;
  const ctx = canvas.getContext('2d');

  // Base shape via path commands (pixel-art style)
  ctx.fillStyle = type === 'boss' ? '#ff0088' : 
                  type === 'elite' ? '#00ffff' : '#00ff00';
  ctx.fillRect(16, 8, 32, 16); // body

  // Eyes (white)
  ctx.fillStyle = '#ffffff';
  if (frameIndex % 2 === 0) {
    ctx.fillRect(20, 12, 4, 4); // left eye open
    ctx.fillRect(40, 12, 4, 4); // right eye open
  } else {
    ctx.fillRect(20, 14, 4, 2); // left eye squint
    ctx.fillRect(40, 14, 4, 2); // right eye squint
  }

  // Antennae (pulse effect)
  const pulse = Math.sin(Date.now() * 0.01 + type) * 2;
  ctx.strokeStyle = '#ffffff';
  ctx.lineWidth = 2;
  ctx.beginPath();
  ctx.moveTo(24, 8);
  ctx.lineTo(24, 8 - pulse);
  ctx.stroke();

  return canvas;
}

// Convert to Three.js texture
const texture = new THREE.CanvasTexture(canvas);
texture.magFilter = THREE.NearestFilter; // pixel-art crispness
texture.minFilter = THREE.NearestFilter;
```

#### Starfield Noise Generation (Simplex-like)
```javascript
function generateStarPositions(count, spread): Vector2[] {
  const stars = [];
  for (let i = 0; i < count; i++) {
    // Pseudo-random via seeded hash
    const seed = i * 12345 + 67890;
    const x = ((seed * 1103515245) % 1000000) / 1000000 * spread - spread/2;
    const y = (((seed * 1103515245) >> 16) % 1000000) / 1000000 * spread - spread/2;

    // Depth-based size and brightness
    const depth = i / count;
    stars.push({ 
      position: new THREE.Vector3(x, y, -50 - depth * 150),
      size: 1 + depth * 2,
      brightness: 0.3 + depth * 0.7
    });
  }
  return stars;
}
```

