## 6. PERFORMANCE BUDGET & MEMORY MANAGEMENT PLAN

### Object Pooling Allocation Table

| Entity Type | Pool Size | Reuse Trigger | Disposal Condition |
|-------------|-----------|---------------|-------------------|
| Player Bullets | 50 | `pool.acquire()` on shoot | Game over, wave reset |
| Alien Bullets | 100 | `pool.acquire()` on alien fire | Game over, wave reset |
| Aliens (InstancedMesh) | 55 instances | Matrix update only | Never disposed during gameplay |
| Particles | 500 max active | LRU strategy in ParticleManager | Explicit `.dispose()` on pool clear |
| Power-Ups | 10 | `pool.acquire()` on spawn | Collected by player, game over |

### Memory Leak Prevention Checklist

- [ ] All geometries/materials/textures created via `new THREE.*` receive `.dispose()` call when removed from scene.
- [ ] Object pools clear all references on game reset (`pool.clear()` calls).
- [ ] Event listeners attached to window/document are removed in `gameLogic.js` cleanup.
- [ ] `EffectComposer` disposed via `composer.dispose()` on page unload.
- [ ] Web Audio API oscillators stopped and disconnected after SFX playback.

### Frame Budget (60 FPS Target)

| Task | Max Time (ms) | Implementation Strategy |
|------|---------------|------------------------|
| Physics Update | 2.0 | AABB collision, no continuous collision detection |
| Render Loop | 8.0 | InstancedMesh for aliens, single particle system |
| Post-Processing | 5.0 | Bloom at 256 resolution, not full screen |
| Input Handling | <0.1 | Polling via `requestAnimationFrame` callback |
| Audio Synthesis | <0.5 | Pre-buffered oscillators, no runtime allocation |

